0010 — wsb_eval.py: accept the official `torch-eager` backend in the standard
      evaluation allowlist.

Repository ownership: WildSongBench (m-a-p/WildSongBench) — the standard-mode
backend allowlist lives in `evaluation/wsb_metrics/wsb_eval.py::verify_inputs`
(the `config.get('backend')` check). This patch is maintained in
AIwork4me/YuE2-SGLang-ROCm until it is submitted upstream (owner approval
required; see upstream/UPSTREAM_PATCHES_2026-11.md).

WHY
---
WildSongBench's own reproduction protocol (benchmark/reproduction_manifest.jsonl,
`code/generate.py`) records the backend used for each candidate. The official
YuE inference package (yue2-infer, pinned by the benchmark) exposes `torch`
(graph-capture) and `torch-eager` (public-SDPA eager) CLI backends; YuE's
official documentation (docs/hardware.md) documents `torch-eager` as the
supported AMD ROCm path. yue2 0.1.3's graph path selects aten varlen
FlashAttention by schema-presence and the ROCm mha_varlen_fwd kernel rejects
`seqused_k` (RuntimeError: [ROCm] mha_varlen_fwd: seqused_k must be nullopt),
so AMD ROCm runs must use `torch-eager`.

The frozen evaluator's standard-mode allowlist is `{'torch', 'vllm'}` and
therefore rejects candidates generated with the officially supported ROCm
backend — a portability defect in the benchmark validation gate, not in the
generation or scoring math.

EXACT CHANGE (one line)
-----------------------
    -    if config.get('backend') not in {'torch', 'vllm'}:
    +    if config.get('backend') not in {'torch', 'vllm', 'torch-eager'}:

WHAT IT DOES NOT TOUCH
----------------------
Generation budgets, seeds, selection rules, scoring formulas, phonemization,
edit distance, aggregation, summaries, and the torch/vllm paths. NVIDIA and
vLLM users are unaffected (their backends remain in the allowlist verbatim).

TESTS
-----
tests/test_evaluator_patches.py rebuilds the full patched tree from the
PRISTINE frozen tarball and asserts, at every stage, the bit-exact hashes
recorded in configs/benchmark.lock.yaml:
  pristine wsb_eval.py          29310259…
  +0006                          6a4a53ed…   (lock-pinned)
  +0009 (cumulative hunk)        729fd597…   (lock: patched_wsb_eval_sha256)
  +0010                          efb89042…   (this patch; recorded in the
                                              evaluator release.json receipts)
Negative controls: allowlist still rejects unknown backends; the 0010 hunk
applies ONLY on top of 0006+0009 (refuses on pristine).

EXPECTED UPSTREAM STATEMENT
---------------------------
WildSongBench standard evaluation: the backend allowlist rejects
`torch-eager`, an official yue2-infer backend and the documented AMD ROCm
path (YuE docs/hardware.md). AMD-generated candidates cannot be scored
without this one-line admission change. Patch adds `torch-eager` to the
allowlist; no scoring semantics are altered.
